== Protocols and information ==
=== Policies ===
{{short|WP:AIPOLICY}}
;<small>AI usage</small>
*''' {{section link|WP:Editing policy#Artificial intelligence additions}}''' - ([[WP:EPAI]]) – the use of  [[Artificial intelligence|AI writing tools]] such as [[Wikipedia:Large language models|large language models]] (LLMs) for the  [[Wikipedia:Writing articles with large language models| creation or rewriting of articles]], or their usage to generate [[Wikipedia:Image use policy#AI-generated images|images]], [[Wikipedia:Reliable sources#Sources produced by machine learning|sources]] or [[Wikipedia:Talk page guidelines#LLM-generated| comments]], save for a few exceptions, is generally prohibited (as outlined by the linked pages below)
;<small>Images</small>
*'''{{section link|WP:Biographies of living persons#AI generated images}}''' - ([[WP:AIIMGBLP]])  – AI-generated images should not be used to depict subjects of BLPs
*'''{{section link|WP:Image use policy#AI-generated images}}'''  - ([[WP:AIIMAGES]])  – most images wholly generated by AI should not be used in mainspace
;<small>Deletion</small>
*'''[[WP:Speedy deletion#G15. LLM-generated pages without human review|WP:Speedy deletion § G15]]''' - ([[WP:G15]])  – for a page that exhibits signs that it was generated by an LLM with no human review

=== Guidelines ===
; <small>Article content</small> 
{{short|WP:AIGUIDELINE}}
* '''[[WP:Writing articles with large language models]]''' - ([[WP:LLM]]) – the use of LLMs to generate or rewrite article content is largely prohibited
* '''[[WP:LLM-assisted translation]]''' - ([[WP:LLMT]]) – about machine translation tools that includes LLMs
;<small>Images</small>
*'''{{section link|WP:Manual of Style/Images#AI upscaling}}''' - ([[MOS:AIUPSCALE]]) – AI-upscaling should  not be used to increase the resolution of images
;<small>Sources</small>
*'''{{section link|WP:Reliable sources#Sources produced by machine learning}}''' - ([[WP:RSML]]) –  sources produced by LLMs are  generally unreliable
;<small>Talk pages</small>
*'''{{section link|WP:Talk page guidelines#LLM}}'''  - ([[WP:AITALK]]) –  about striking or collapsing comments that are generated by AI-technology
;<small>Behavioral</small>
*'''{{section link|WP:Disruptive editing#Persistent LLM use}}'''  - ([[WP:LLMDISRUPT]]) –  repeated use of LLMs to generate content is considered disruptive
;<small>Deletion</small>
*'''[[WP:Presumptive removal of AI-generated content]]''' - ([[WP:LLMPRV]]) – AI generated contributions to pages may be reversed, and single-contributor pages may be deleted

